    "chapter_label": "Microorganisms: friend and foe",
    "subtopic_id": "science/grade_08/ch_02/H008",
    "stem": "Nila mixes a drop of pond water and a little moist soil with water. With unaided eyes she sees nothing living. Under a microscope she sees tiny moving beings and also tiny living beings that stay still.\n\nWhich statements are correct?",
    "item_type": "three_statement",
    "options": {
      "A": "1 and 3 only",
      "B": "1 and 2 only",
      "C": "2 and 3 only",
      "D": "1, 2 and 3"
    },
    "statements": [
      {
        "id": "1",
        "text": "Those tiny living beings are microorganisms because they are living and too small for the unaided eye."
      },
      {
        "id": "2",
        "text": "A nonliving soil grain seen only under the microscope is a microorganism."
      },
      {
        "id": "3",
        "text": "Tiny living beings that stay still under the microscope are still microorganisms if they are living and too small for the unaided eye."
      }
